# Pins for `public-api-deps.txt`, the committed manifest of foreign crates
# reachable from this crate's public API. The `sdk-public-api` CI job reads
# both values out of here, so this is the single source of truth — the
# workflow does not repeat them.
#
# Both pins matter: `cargo public-api`'s listing is the input the manifest is
# derived from, and anything that changes the *rendering* can change which
# paths the extraction sees.
#
#   toolchain  — rustdoc's JSON format changes shape across nightlies.
#   tool       — `cargo public-api`'s own rendering changes across releases.
#
# Regenerate with exactly these:
#
#   rustup toolchain install nightly-2026-05-05
#   cargo install cargo-public-api --locked --version 0.52.0
#   cargo +nightly-2026-05-05 public-api -p bitrouter-sdk --all-features --simplified \
#     | grep -oE '\b[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*(::[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)+' \
#     | cut -d: -f1 | sort -u \
#     | grep -vxE 'bitrouter_sdk|core|std|alloc'
#
# Append the result under the comment header in `public-api-deps.txt`; the
# header is stripped before comparison, so keep it out of the generated part.
#
# Run it on Linux or macOS. `bitrouter-sdk` has `#[cfg(unix)]` items, so a
# Windows-generated listing will not match; the CI job runs on Linux.
#
# Because the manifest is a set of crate names rather than a byte-for-byte
# listing, moving either pin is far less disruptive than it used to be:
# rendering churn no longer rewrites the file, and only a genuine change in
# the public dependency surface produces a diff.
toolchain=nightly-2026-05-05
tool=cargo-public-api@0.52.0
